On their own it is close enough to a toss-up that it may not be worth
calculating the exact damage per hit.  But they have other side effects.

Demonbane is a long sword.  If you got it as a gift you can get to at
least Basic skill in long swords.  The second best weapon in the game
is Frost Bane that is an unaligned long sword.  Far more sacraficing
and you may end up with Frost Bane.

Werebane is a silver saber.  If you got it as a gift you ca get to at
least Basic skill in silver sabers.  The best weapon in the games is
Greyswandir that is a lawfull silver saber.  Far more sacraficing and
you may end up with Greyswandir.  And just in case your character
class can two-weapon, doing so with Werebane and a regular silver saber
makes short work of demons in Gehennom.

Since you appear to be lawfull, it is reasonable to expect that you
could get either of the two better weaspons if you return up to an
altar.

Back to on their own, Werebanse is inherrently rustproof from being
silver, Demonbane needs to be rustproofed by hand.

